OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ADolly Parton was the one thing most
OL,4,AAmericans could agree on
OL,5,
OL,6,FDolly Parton was a lot of things - a
OL,7,Fcountry musician, a philanthropist, an
OL,8,Factress, a storyteller and a
OL,9,Fbusinesswoman. One thing she never was,
OL,10,Fhowever, was a politician.
OL,12,FBut don't think it's because no one
OL,13,Fasked her. In 1999, during an
OL,14,Fappearance on the talk show Prime Time
OL,15,FCountry!, the singer was asked by a
OL,16,Fyoung woman in the audience if she
OL,17,Fwould ever run for office.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,169,160,200,105,0,100
PN,16802
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F168A1787747055
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ADolly Parton was the one thing most
OL,4,AAmericans could agree on
OL,5,
OL,6,FDolly demurred, with her characteristic
OL,7,Frazor-sharp wit. "I think of myself
OL,8,Fmore as a diplomat. That's the kind of
OL,9,Fpeople who tell you to go to hell in
OL,10,Fsuch a way you look forward to the
OL,11,Ftrip."
OL,13,FIt's something she'd had to do many
OL,14,Ftimes over a career that spanned
OL,15,Fdecades and genres. With a fanbase that
OL,16,Fincluded grandmas and Gen-Zers,
OL,17,FRepublicans and Democrats, drag queens
OL,18,Fand evangelicals, Parton was a kind of
OL,19,Funicorn in America's polarised society.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
